<title>AUSTRALIA: Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - July 10.</title>
<headline>Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - July 10.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Wednesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name			P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	 394.06   7.96</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	   212.50   1.02</p>
<p> 3   Syd Hrbr Casino	171.90   2.08</p>
<p> 4   Ranger Minerals	170.67   3.55</p>
<p> 5   Perilya Mines	  134.15   0.55</p>
<p> 6   Westpac Prop Tr	111.87   1.79</p>
<p> 7   Tap Oil		   85.23   1.50</p>
<p> 8   Consol Paper	    79.41   2.70</p>
<p> 9   Broken Hill Pty	 72.76  18.96</p>
<p>10   Western Metals	  71.93   1.23</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining	    1.73   0.86</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    3.70   0.83</p>
<p> 3   Jardine Fm China	 5.20   0.77</p>
<p> 4   Haoma Mining	     5.97   0.30</p>
<p> 5   RGC			  6.05   4.12</p>
<p> 6   Mt Leyshon Gold	  6.88   1.60</p>
<p> 7   Gwalia Consol	    6.99   1.35</p>
<p> 8   Croesus Min		7.00   0.35</p>
<p> 9   McPhersons		 7.10   2.47</p>
<p>10   Australian Resc	  7.51   0.44</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
